  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAC-Raising awareness on Cybersecurity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Legal consultancy for poor people and Community Development Center&#x2019;s (LAC) initiative aims to address the issue of network information security, electronic transactions for women, children, poor people, and the ethnicity in Ba Vi, Phuc Tho districts,Hanoi. The project&apos;s overall objective is to ensure the right of the people to assess information fast, correctly, and lawfully, contributingto promote digital government, digital economy, and digital society in line with the development orientation of the state. In specific, the Center will approach the beneficiaries to improve their skills in screening, using and exploiting information effectively to best serve their work and study. Furthermore, the initiative will focus on enhancing skills and understanding of legal electronic transactions, promoting the sale and promotion of products. If people know how to promote and trade products on the internet which can reach and approach more customers, it will improve the family&apos;s economic life and contributeto poverty reduction. Additionally, the Center also desires to raise legal awareness for the targeted groups, contributes to preventing the illegal transmission of information, law violation online, preventing acts of interference, access, harm, deletion, change, copying, falsifying information online illegally. The outcomes of the project are expected to be: raising legal awareness for 600 people, providing legal consultation, communication and other legal services for 4.000 people.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&apos;- Since its establishment in 2004 (re-registered under 2008 Decree 77 on Legal Consultancy), the Center has been operating and notviolating the law during its operation. The Center has accomplished legal consultancy and communication for thousands of people whovisit our office. Our beneficiaries are among women, the poor, families under preferential treatment policy, people in minor ethniccommunities and remote areas, the homeless elderly, the vulnerable ...
- Within 10 consecutive years from 2008- 2018, the Center has implemented 3 phases of the project, funded by DANIDA-Denmark to provide mobile legal aid for ethnic minorities in Hoa Binh, Son La, Dien Bien, Lai Chau and Lao Provinces. The Center has organized 2,096 mobile legal aid campaign for 94,332 locals in different villages, approximately 500 legal training courses for our collaborators and beyond. In 2015 - 2018, the Center carried out a legal consultancy project on cooperative contracts for local people and businesses, including legal consultancy on labor contracts, employment, insurance for employees in companies and factories in Lao Cai, Lai Chau and Son La provinces.
- In cooperation with the Center for Women and Development, the Center implemented community-based mobile legal consultancy projects funded by VUSTA and UNICEF. In particular, the UNICEF-funded project, Forum Lawyers and Children, implemented in 5 provinces across Vietnam, has spread humane valuesto children living on the streets and in nurturing centers, and reformatoryschools.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center of Legal Advice for Poor Peo</narrative>
